[FILES_REFERENCE]
overview: Where to put different types of information
purpose: Route discovered knowledge to correct documentation file
principle: Each file has specific scope - don't mix concerns

[FILE_CLAUDE_MD]
location: /CLAUDE.md (root of project)
scope: Critical universal rules (apply to ALL work on project)
examples_update:
  - "Never use FFI without validating all pointers"
  - "No raw delete/new outside RAII constructors"
  - "All C++ code must be snake_case"
  - "Core MUST NOT write to filesystem"
examples_not:
  - Layer-specific rules (→ CONSTRAINTS.toon)
  - Algorithm details (→ CRYPTO.toon)
  - Implementation patterns (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Module responsibilities (→ MODULES.toon)
when_update: Rare. Only if affects ALL code in project.
format: Markdown section under "⚠️ СТРОГИЕ ПРАВИЛА"
size: Keep small (root file should be quick to read)

[FILE_CONSTRAINTS_TOON]
location: docs/agent/CONSTRAINTS.toon
scope: Architectural constraints and "never do this" rules
examples_update:
  - [CONSTRAINT_N]: "weak_ptr only between Layer 2 and Layer 4"
  - [CONSTRAINT_N]: "Layer N cannot call Layer N-1"
  - [CONSTRAINT_N]: "No allocations > 64MB in single block"
  - [CONSTRAINT_N]: "Thread safety required for Layer 2+ shared state"
examples_not:
  - Implementation details (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - What layers do (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - How modules interact (→ MODULES.toon)
  - Key sizes or algorithms (→ CRYPTO.toon)
when_update: When discovering "you must not" or "only between X and Y"
format: [CONSTRAINT_N] section + rule + why + how_to_apply
size: Comprehensive but focused (one constraint = 5-10 lines max)

[FILE_ARCHITECTURE_TOON]
location: docs/agent/ARCHITECTURE.toon
scope: Layer structure, dataflow, component interactions
examples_update:
  - How data flows through layers
  - What each layer owns vs observes
  - Caching patterns (Layer 4 LRU for Layer 2 objects)
  - Concurrency model per layer
  - State machine transitions
examples_not:
  - Constraints (→ CONSTRAINTS.toon)
  - Specific algorithms (→ CRYPTO.toon)
  - Module purposes (→ MODULES.toon)
  - Crypto details (→ CRYPTO.toon)
when_update: When understanding layer interactions or data movement
format: Structured text with [LAYER_N] sections
size: Medium (should fit in one document)

[FILE_CRYPTO_TOON]
location: docs/agent/CRYPTO.toon
scope: Cryptographic components, algorithms, key management
examples_update:
  - "ChaCha20 nonce is now counter-based, not random"
  - "Key rotation happens every 30 days (found in code)"
  - "Ed25519 conversion to X25519 uses clamping"
  - "Shared secret uses HKDF-SHA256 for KDF"
examples_not:
  - Layer constraints (→ CONSTRAINTS.toon)
  - Architecture details (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Module responsibilities (→ MODULES.toon)
when_update: When learning about cryptographic implementation
format: [ALGO.X] or [COMPONENT_Y] sections with details
size: Reference document (comprehensive)

[FILE_MODULES_TOON]
location: docs/agent/MODULES.toon
scope: Module responsibilities, what they own, how they work
examples_update:
  - "Client now caches pubkeys in SQLite, doesn't fetch each time"
  - "Core_engine owns all 5 layer managers via shared_ptr"
  - "Relay statelessness: no session storage except in-memory transient"
  - "Module X exports these 5 functions via FFI"
examples_not:
  - Algorithms (→ CRYPTO.toon)
  - Layer structure (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
  - Constraints (→ CONSTRAINTS.toon)
when_update: When understanding module structure or responsibilities
format: [MODULE.X] sections with subsections for structure/responsibility
size: Reference document

[FILE_ACTIVE_EPICS_TOON]
location: docs/agent/ACTIVE_EPICS.toon
scope: Current work status, epic progress, blockers
examples_update:
  - "EPIC-10 status changed from IN_PROGRESS to BLOCKED (waiting EPIC-15)"
  - "EPIC-11 now partially complete (rooms work, members in progress)"
  - "New blocker: EPIC-4 depends on EPIC-3 (ECDH)"
examples_not:
  - Code details (→ MODULES.toon)
  - Constraints (→ CONSTRAINTS.toon)
  - Architecture (→ ARCHITECTURE.toon)
when_update: When discovering epic status from code or user
format: [EPIC_N] sections with status, dependencies, deliverables
size: Status board (changes frequently)

[DECISION_MATRIX]
Information Type → File

Critical rule (all code)
  → CLAUDE.md

"Never do X" / Architecture limit
  → CONSTRAINTS.toon

How layers interact / dataflow
  → ARCHITECTURE.toon

Cryptographic algorithm / key management
  → CRYPTO.toon

Module owns what / FFI exports / inter-module
  → MODULES.toon

Epic status / blockers / progress
  → ACTIVE_EPICS.toon

Unknown file → QUICK_LINKS.toon (says which file)
